# Copy to .env and fill in for local dev, or set these in the real
# deployment's environment (see docker-compose.yml / server/README.md for
# the self-hosted deployment's full variable list, including optional
# integrations like Gmail and Google Calendar).
#
# The variables below are enforced by src/lib/server/boot-checks.ts: the
# SvelteKit server refuses to start in production if any is missing. They
# are NOT enforced under `npm run dev` (vite dev) — see the `if (!dev)`
# guard in src/hooks.server.ts — so local dev works without this file, but
# a few features (dashboard login, signed game links) fall back to
# less-safe dev-only defaults and warn on the console until you set these.

# Absolute site origin used to build links that go out in emails (booking
# confirmations, portal links). Unset, these used to leak the raw server IP
# or link to the literal string "undefined".
SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# HMAC signing key for dashboard session cookies AND signed game/homework
# links (src/lib/server/auth.ts, src/lib/server/urls.ts). Unset, both fall
# back to a secret generated fresh at process start, so every restart logs
# everyone out and silently invalidates every game link already sent.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# Tutor dashboard login password. Unset, every login attempt fails, which
# looks like a broken password rather than missing config.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# adapter-node's request origin — see
# https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/adapter-node#Environment-variables-ORIGIN.
# Required so the login cookie's `secure` flag is derived correctly instead
# of depending on an unconfigured default.
ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Must be exactly `x-forwarded-proto` (boot-checks validates the VALUE, not
# just presence — a typo'd or wrong-name header passes a presence-only
# check but fails silently at request time). adapter-node's equivalent of
# Express's `app.set('trust proxy', 1)` — tells it to trust the
# x-forwarded-proto header a reverse proxy (Caddy) sets, instead of
# hardcoding 'https' regardless of the real scheme. See the comment on the
# cookies.set(...) call in src/routes/api/login/+server.ts.
PROTOCOL_HEADER=x-forwarded-proto

# Absolute directory generated content (lesson slides, game data, drafts,
# portal files) is read from and written to (src/lib/server/content.ts).
# Unset, it falls back to the CWD-relative "./data", and adapter-node's
# runtime cwd is not guaranteed to be the repo root. Must exist and be
# writable by the process.
DATA_DIR=./data

# Optional. Path to (or name of, if on PATH) the Claude Code CLI binary
# lesson generation shells out to. Checked at boot but only WARNS if not
# runnable — the site still serves pages and takes bookings, only lesson
# generation fails. Defaults to 'claude'.
#CLAUDE_BIN=claude

# Shared secret the two timer-driven endpoints check for (POST
# /api/reports/prompt, GET /api/remind) — see src/lib/server/cron-auth.ts
# and server/README.md's scheduling section. Unset, both endpoints are
# closed to everyone, timer included, rather than open to anyone.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_KEY=

# Where the daily generation health check (POST /api/health/generation,
# server/meabeclick-generation-health.timer) sends its ONE summary when a
# lesson generation failed, stuck, the engine is down, or a booked maths
# lesson has no ready lesson. Every channel set here gets it.
#
# Recommended: a Slack Incoming Webhook into #meabeclick (Slack app →
# Incoming Webhooks → Add New Webhook). The URL IS the credential: keep it
# here only; the app never logs or returns it.
#OPS_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
#
# Optional second channel: Lior's WhatsApp via CallMeBot (unofficial, free,
# personal use; use a personal number, NOT a WhatsApp Business one — see
# server/README.md). Message the CallMeBot bot "I allow callmebot to send me
# messages" from that phone, then set both. Phone in international digits,
# no + (e.g. 9725XXXXXXXX).
#OPS_CALLMEBOT_PHONE=
#OPS_CALLMEBOT_API_KEY=
#
# With no OPS_ channel the alert falls back to the tutor channel
# (CALLMEBOT_API_KEY); with nothing at all the check answers 503 and its
# timer fails every day, on purpose.
#
# How far back and ahead booked maths lessons must have a ready lesson
# (and how long Codex may go without a success while one is missing).
#GENERATION_HEALTH_STALE_DAYS=3
